# WL-GOV-006 — Legacy Import Archive Standard

## Status

Active

## Purpose

Large legacy Wonderland trees must not become authoritative by accident.

Legacy material must be inventoried, classified, archived, or promoted through review.

## Legacy Source

```text
/Volumes/T7_Wonderland/Wonderland-v4
Authority Root
/Users/wonderland/Wonderland
Rule

Legacy files are evidence until promoted.

They are not authority.

Classification States
archive

Historical material retained for reference.

candidate

Potentially useful material requiring review.

promote

Approved for controlled import into authority root.

reject

Deprecated, duplicate, unsafe, or irrelevant.

Required Import Gates

A legacy item may be promoted only if it has:

Inventory record
Classification
Destination path
Promotion intent
Backup before import
Verification after import
Rollback path
Prohibited

The following may not be bulk-copied from legacy into authority:

bin/
tools/
vault/
services/
.git/
secrets
runtime state
container volumes
caches
Principle

Runtime state is disposable.
Authority is not.
